11497	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s3","entry":{"id":"review-fb4cd145fce88e74c0e02646ba5e1a37","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T11:10:57.228Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"DEF s3 ac1–ac7 are each designed, and the common-class default 'auto' (common tools do not ask by default) is consistent with the user's recorded decision on ac6.","evidence":"DEF.md:138-144 lists ac1–ac7; LLD §2/§5/§6 cover each. docs/plans/tool-registry.md:116 'Default for the flag: `auto` (confirmed by the user)… a common call asks in manual and edit-auto, and does not ask in auto. A destructive call asks in every mode'. The DEF ac6 text itself is not amended; the LLD records this in §10. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"None for the design; the DEF ac6 wording amendment still needs filing as the HLD deferred question says.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"A chat's edits mode reaches the executor as ToolDeps.approvalMode, set by the entry point, so ac6 ('in … a chat alike') holds for chat-originated calls.","evidence":"Today no chat path reaches executeTool: the only executeTool caller is src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts:78 (used by analyze driver and ollama review loop); the chat runs the claude CLI with PermissionMode mapped to CLI flags (vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:79). The LLD's carrier relies on 'the daemon tool-call IPC entry', which §10 says is owned by s7 and left to the plan. No design states how a chat session's mode is attached to a tool call. [files: src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts]","action":"Design the carrier in s3: name the IPC method (or field on an existing one) that brings the chat session's PermissionMode with the call, or state explicitly that s7's tool-call IPC must carry approvalMode and add it as an sc4 requirement on s7.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"executeTool treats requiresApproval (boolean or predicate) as approved, logs 'auto-approving' and runs the tool.","evidence":"src/daemon/tools/executor.ts:41-48: `const needsGate = tool.requiresApproval === true || (typeof tool.requiresApproval === 'function' && tool.requiresApproval(input)); if (needsGate) { log.warn(... 'auto-approving'); }` then `return await tool.execute(input, deps)`. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Eight builtins set destructive: true; IpcStreamKind already has 'gate'; gate.request-permission is an offline stub.","evidence":"grep `destructive: true` hits exactly az/vm.ts:238, aws/s3.ts:210, aws/cloudformation.ts:235, aws/ec2.ts:255, gcp/storage.ts:189, gcp/compute.ts:247, gcp/run.ts:212, k8s/index.ts:340. src/shared/types.ts:905 includes 'gate'. src/daemon/index.ts:1931 `'gate.request-permission': offlineStream(...)`. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/shared/types.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The daemon config key tools.commonApproval is new and no existing approval setting overlaps it.","evidence":"src/daemon/tools/config.ts already holds a ToolSettings snapshot with `approval: { defaultAction: 'approve' | 'skip'; maxEditRounds; showStructuredDiff }` and `destructive: { requireDoubleConfirm: boolean }`, pushed by the `tools.config.set` RPC (src/daemon/index.ts:1708-1716). The LLD names only `src/config` as the call site and never says what happens to approval.defaultAction or destructive.requireDoubleConfirm, which become a second, conflicting approval surface (a 'destructive' setting is exactly what ac5 says must not alter the destructive path). [files: src/daemon/tools/config.ts, src/daemon/index.ts, src/config/config-catalog.ts]","action":"State in §3.5 whether tools.commonApproval lives in src/config/config-catalog.ts or in the ToolSettings snapshot, and retire or map approval.defaultAction and destructive.requireDoubleConfirm (or state they are unread).","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Reused pieces exist with the stated shape: ToolApprovalGate/buildApprovalGate as preview source, and a stream subscription pattern on the server.","evidence":"src/daemon/tools/types.ts:83-94 ToolApprovalGate {title, content, actions}; :145 buildApprovalGate?(input). src/daemon/index.ts:1937 'todos.subscribe' is a live stream subscription handler that approval.subscribe can follow. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The four ToolDeps builders (driver.ts, ollama.ts, grounding.ts, changed-files.ts) are executor paths where setting caller/approvalMode governs approval.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts:370-371 and src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts:110-111 build ToolDeps and call `gitDiffTool.execute(...)` directly, bypassing executeTool, so no approval step runs for them whatever caller is set. Only driver.ts (via runReadOnlyToolLoop) and ollama.ts:681-686 go through executeTool. [files: src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"Note that direct tool.execute calls bypass the gate (harmless for read-only git_diff today) and either route them through executeTool or leave them to s7's typed-helper move with an explicit statement; drop the claim that setting caller there affects approval.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Every use of requiresApproval/destructive is in the builtins and is changed in the builtin mapping step.","evidence":"src/docgen/tool.ts:56 declares `requiresApproval: false` on a Tool outside src/daemon/tools/builtins; step 5 maps 'every builtin' and the contract test checks 'no builtin', so step 6's removal of the field from the Tool type breaks compilation there. [files: src/docgen/tool.ts]","action":"Add src/docgen/tool.ts (and any other non-builtin Tool) to the §3.1 call sites and step 5.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Nothing is persisted: the pending table is in memory and a restart denies open requests; the Tool-type change has no outside consumer.","evidence":"The design adds no stored record; the pending table and stream set are in-memory (§3.4). The IDE repo is deprecated (project memory), and the Tool type is only implemented in this repo (grep for requiresApproval only hits src/). [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"s3 stays within sc4 and does not redesign another Story's surface.","evidence":"Migration step 6 says s3 sets caller and approvalMode 'at the daemon tool-call IPC entry', while §10 says that IPC is 'owned by s7' and left to the plan; docs/plans/tool-registry.md:105 says the method's shape and caller value are 's3 and s7 design'. The LLD both builds into it and disclaims it, and s7 depends on s3, so step 6 cannot touch an IPC that s7 has not built yet. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Decide one owner: either s3 defines the tool-call IPC's caller/approvalMode fields as part of sc4 (and s7 builds the method against them), or step 6 drops the IPC entry and s7 carries it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"When a subscriber's socket closes, the server aborts its stream handler's signal, so the broker can detect zero open streams.","evidence":"src/daemon/server.ts:260-267: `const abortController = new AbortController(); const onClose = () => { abortController.abort(); }; socket.on('close', onClose); socket.on('error', onError);` and the signal is passed to the handler at :282. [files: src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Denials are returned as s2's ToolFailure kind 'denied' with ToolDenialReason, and executeTool still never throws.","evidence":"S002/LLD.md:61 'denied comes from the approval step of s3'; :202 and :331 add ToolFailure, ToolFailureKind and ToolDenialReason. executor.ts:47-58 catches every throw into a success:false ToolResult; the LLD keeps that invariant. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S002/LLD.md, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"None; build s3 after s2 step 1 lands the types.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to a proving test.","evidence":"§6 acceptance mapping lists tests for ac1–ac7 across approval-broker, approval-ipc, executor-approval and approval-class-mapping test files, covering no-client, timeout, decline, every-mode destructive and late subscriber.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.2","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"ac6's client side ('asks … in the terminal client, the editor and a chat alike') and ac7's 'client can show the exact call' are proved by a test.","evidence":"Migration step 4 adds approval.subscribe/answer to the TUI, the editor plugin and the chat, but the test strategy's subjects and acceptance mapping are all daemon-side (broker, executor, server IPC); no test exercises the TUI, the vscode-plugin daemon client (vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts) or the chat panel rendering and answering a gate frame. [files: vscode-plugin/src/daemon/controller.ts]","action":"Add client-level tests (TUI service and plugin client: receives a gate frame, shows tool/repo/arguments, sends approval.answer) to the ac6 and ac7 rows.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":6,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T11:10:57.228Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
