13671	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s3","entry":{"id":"review-63ec4aa27e21f188d2f3f176e7a68c14","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T11:15:39.537Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The common class follows a global flag (manual | edit-auto | auto, default auto) that a chat's edits mode overrides per call, and the destructive class asks in every mode, as the user decided.","evidence":"docs/plans/tool-registry.md:114-116 'Decision: global flag as the default, the chat edits mode overrides it': three values manual/edit-auto/auto, default auto, common asks in manual and edit-auto, destructive asks in every mode. LLD §3.2, §3.5 and the edge-case table match this. DEF S003 ac6 (DEF.md:143) says such tools 'ask ... before it runs'. Under the default auto they do not ask, but the later user decision deliberately covers that, and LLD §10 records the reading. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The eight builtins that set destructive: true map to the destructive class, and the LLD says how buildApprovalGate relates to the request (HLD finding 3 / decision).","evidence":"The grep finds destructive: true at az/vm.ts:238, aws/s3.ts:210, aws/cloudformation.ts:235, aws/ec2.ts:255, gcp/storage.ts:189, gcp/compute.ts:247, gcp/run.ts:212 and k8s/index.ts:340, which is exactly eight. LLD §2.3/§2.4 map them to destructive and keep buildApprovalGate as the preview source. tool-registry.md:118-120 requires both. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"executeTool treats requiresApproval (true or a predicate) as approved, logs 'auto-approving' and runs the tool (executor.ts:41-48).","evidence":"executor.ts:41-45: `const needsGate = tool.requiresApproval === true || (typeof tool.requiresApproval === 'function' && tool.requiresApproval(input)); if (needsGate) { log.warn(..., 'tool requires approval but the gate dispatcher is gone; auto-approving'); }` and then `return await tool.execute(input, deps)` at line 48. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The IPC server pushes to a client only over a stream the client opened, aborts the handler signal when the socket closes, IpcStreamKind already lists 'gate', and gate.request-permission is an offline stub.","evidence":"server.ts:261-267 creates an AbortController per stream request and aborts it on socket 'close'/'error'. shared/types.ts:905 `IpcStreamKind = 'delta' | 'progress' | 'gate' | ...`. index.ts:1931 `'gate.request-permission': offlineStream('gate.request-permission')`. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/shared/types.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"approval.defaultAction and destructive.requireDoubleConfirm are read by nothing outside src/daemon/tools/config.ts.","evidence":"The grep for defaultAction|requireDoubleConfirm|defaultApproval finds hits only in config.ts (lines 30, 50, 74, 79, 109, 129, 147). getToolSettings() callers read only shell, web and notify settings (shell/exec.ts:64, web/index.ts:66, notify/index.ts). [files: src/daemon/tools/config.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The broker, approval.subscribe and approval.answer are new. No approval exchange exists today, and the reused ToolApprovalGate/buildApprovalGate has the stated shape (title, content, actions).","evidence":"There is no 'approval.' handler in index.ts. 'gate.resolve' (index.ts:1913) and 'gate.request-permission' (index.ts:1931) are offline stubs. types.ts:83-94 `interface ToolApprovalGate { title: string; content: string; actions: ReadonlyArray<Record<string, unknown>> }`. tool-registry.md:20 confirms 'no approval exchange over IPC exists'. [files: src/daemon/index.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The chat's PermissionMode uses the same three values as approvalMode (manual | edit-auto | auto), so a chat can send it unchanged.","evidence":"vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts:79 `export type PermissionMode = 'manual' | 'edit-auto' | 'auto';` and chat-panel.ts:236 keeps it per session. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/protocol.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Mapping rule: 'every requiresApproval flag becomes common' (§2.3, migration step 5, and the contract test 'every builtin that had requiresApproval maps to common or a per-input class').","evidence":"There are 77 `requiresApproval: false` declarations across 55 files, all on read-only tools: git/status.ts, git/diff.ts, git/log.ts, file/read.ts, search/grep.ts, search/glob.ts, graph/index.ts (4), docs/index.ts (4), gh/pr.ts (5), and src/docgen/tool.ts, among others. src/docgen/tool.ts, which the LLD names as 'the one Tool outside the builtins that declares requiresApproval', declares it false. Built as written, the mapping step and its contract test turn every read-only tool into common. Under manual or edit-auto those tools would then ask, and with no client attached the read-only analyze and review loops (read-only-tool-loop.ts via driver.ts and ollama.ts:681) would be denied. The rule must state that `true` maps to common, a predicate maps to a per-input function returning common or none, and `false` or absent maps to none, and the contract test must assert that. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins/git/status.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/file/read.ts, src/docgen/tool.ts, src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts]","action":"Restate the mapping as true → common, predicate → per-input (common | none), false/absent → none. Add a contract test that every former requiresApproval:false tool resolves to none.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Only src/analyze/context/driver.ts and src/agent/providers/ollama.ts build ToolDeps that reach executeTool. grounding.ts and changed-files.ts call git_diff's execute directly.","evidence":"The only executeTool caller outside the executor is read-only-tool-loop.ts:78. It is reached from driver.ts:875 (deps from buildToolDeps at driver.ts:1114-1133) and ollama.ts:681-686. grounding.ts:370-371 and changed-files.ts:110-111 call `gitDiffTool.execute(...)` directly. [files: src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, src/analyze/context/driver.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts, src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The config key for the common-class flag is named consistently across the design.","evidence":"§3.5 and migration step 2 name it `approval.commonMode` in ToolSettings. §6 test subject says 'config reader for tools.commonApproval', and §7 'State after' says 'The common class follows tools.commonApproval (default auto)'. config.ts reads dotted keys such as incoming['approval.defaultAction'], so a mismatched name silently keeps the default. [files: src/daemon/tools/config.ts]","action":"Pick one key (approval.commonMode fits config.ts's dotted keys) and use it in §6 and §7.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.4","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The client-side call sites for approval.subscribe are covered by src/shared/ipc-client.ts and src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts.","evidence":"src/shared/ipc-client.ts has only the unary rpc() and the IpcClient interface (rpc/status/reachability/update/updateOutcome, lines 121-138), with no stream method. The vscode-plugin reaches the daemon through this IpcClient (extension.ts:15), so a stream API has to be added there, and the LLD does not say so. src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts is the MCP process, which is not a human client that answers approvals. The terminal-client (src/cli/...) and vscode-plugin chat/editor files that must open the stream and answer are not listed, although §6 names tests at src/cli/services/__tests__ and vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts, src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts]","action":"Add to §3.6: a streaming method on IpcClient in src/shared/ipc-client.ts, plus the TUI service and the vscode-plugin chat/editor modules that subscribe and answer. Drop or justify src/mcp/daemon-stream.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Removing approval.defaultAction and destructive.requireDoubleConfirm, and adding the new key, is safe for older clients that still push the old keys. No stored data is rewritten.","evidence":"updateToolSettings (config.ts:106-150) reads named keys from an untyped record and ignores the rest, so an older client pushing 'approval.defaultAction' is harmless once the field is removed. ToolSettings is an in-memory snapshot (config.ts:93) with no persistence, and the broker's pending table is in memory by design (§3.4). [files: src/daemon/tools/config.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"s3 does not build s7's tool-call IPC. It only defines that method's caller and approvalMode request fields as part of sc4, and leaves the direct-execute builders to s7.","evidence":"tool-registry.md:105: 'The IPC method's shape and its caller value (see finding 4) are s3 and s7 design.' LLD §4 says s7 builds the method against fields s3 defines, and migration step 6 leaves grounding.ts and changed-files.ts to s7. Approval runs at step 2 before s1's hook stage and returns s2's ToolFailure kind 'denied' (HLD.md:131-132) without redefining either. [files: docs/plans/tool-registry.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Caller-signal abort: 'the executor returns an aborted failure and the tool does not run'. The failure is detectable by a stated kind.","evidence":"The shared failure kinds s2 owns are HLD.md:131 `ToolFailureKind = 'missing-tool' | 'missing-signin' | 'unreachable' | 'timed-out' | 'rejected' | 'conversion-failed' | 'schema-mismatch' | 'denied'`, and there is no 'aborted' kind. s2's LLD handles its own abort as 'retries-exhausted' with detail 'cancelled' (S002/LLD.md:253-254). The ApprovalDenial union (declined | timed-out | no-client) has no cancel value either, so the LLD never says which ToolFailure kind or denial reason an aborted approval returns. [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/HLD.md, docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/S002/LLD.md]","action":"State the kind for an aborted approval: for example 'denied' with a new ToolDenialReason 'cancelled' (an sc4/sc5 field change), or an existing kind with a detail. Add it to the broker's unit test subjects.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac1 to ac7 maps to at least one named test in a file under the repo's node:test/tsx convention, including the client-side clauses of ac6 and ac7.","evidence":"The §6 acceptance mapping names tests for ac1 to ac7. The daemon tests are under src/daemon/tools/__tests__, which the CLAUDE.md sweep 'src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts' runs. The editor/chat test is vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/approval-subscribe.test.ts, which matches vscode-plugin/package.json:841 `\"test\": \"tsx --test 'src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts'\"`; that directory already holds tests such as approval-queue.test.ts. [files: vscode-plugin/package.json]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":3,"low":11,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T11:15:39.537Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
