13118	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s3","entry":{"id":"review-e065a4ebb517ae94aad693697e4ca928","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T11:52:23.157Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of DEF s3 ac1–ac7 is designed, and ac6 is read as the user decided: a common call asks in manual and edit-auto, a destructive call always asks, and the global flag defaults to auto.","evidence":"DEF.md:138-144 lists ac1–ac7. docs/plans/tool-registry.md, section 'Decision: global flag as the default, the chat edits mode overrides it', says: 'A destructive call asks in every mode ... Default for the flag: `auto` (confirmed by the user)'. The LLD's §2.2 postconditions, §3.5 and its acceptance mapping cover every criterion, and DEF S003:FR001 (repository and arguments) is in ApprovalRequest (§3.3). [files: docs/epics/one-tool-registry-git-gh-jira-E20261023b7a68147/DEF.md, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Open question 'R2 follow-up': the sc2 and sc3 amendments that s2 requires were not filed in this run.","evidence":"Both amendments exist. .insrc/artifacts/AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-6.json has contractId sc2, 'outputSchema is a typebox TSchema; TypedTool; callTool signature'. AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-7.json has contractId sc3, 'convertText takes ToolDeps; keyValues required'. tool-registry.md R2 requires them to be filed in the s3 run, so this open question is out of date and would send the plan to file duplicates. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-6.json, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-7.json, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"Remove or correct the R2 open question: name AMD-6 (sc2) and AMD-7 (sc3) as filed and pending approval.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"executeTool treats requiresApproval (true or a predicate) as approved, logs 'auto-approving' and runs the tool (executor.ts:41-48).","evidence":"executor.ts:41-45: `const needsGate = tool.requiresApproval === true || (typeof tool.requiresApproval === 'function' && tool.requiresApproval(input)); if (needsGate) { log.warn(..., 'tool requires approval but the gate dispatcher is gone; auto-approving'); }`, then line 48 is `return await tool.execute(input, deps)`. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Exactly eight builtins set destructive: true.","evidence":"A grep for `destructive:\\s*true` finds 8 files: az/vm.ts:238, aws/s3.ts:210, aws/cloudformation.ts:235, aws/ec2.ts:255, gcp/storage.ts:189, gcp/compute.ts:247, gcp/run.ts:212 and k8s/index.ts:340. Nothing reads `tool.destructive`; tool-surface.ts:17 mentions it only in a comment. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/builtins/k8s/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The server can push to a client only over a stream the client opened, and it aborts the handler's signal when the socket closes. IpcStreamKind already has 'gate', and gate.request-permission is an offline stub.","evidence":"server.ts:260-267 creates an AbortController per stream and aborts it on socket 'close' and 'error'; sendStream writes only to the requesting socket. shared/types.ts:905 IpcStreamKind includes 'gate'. index.ts:1931 has `'gate.request-permission': offlineStream('gate.request-permission')`. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/shared/types.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Of the four ToolDeps builders, only driver.ts and ollama.ts reach executeTool. grounding.ts and changed-files.ts call a tool's execute directly.","evidence":"Neither driver.ts nor ollama.ts calls executeTool directly. They reach it through runReadOnlyToolLoop (driver.ts:875, ollama.ts:681), which calls `executeTool(name, input as never, deps)` at read-only-tool-loop.ts:78; that is the only production caller. grounding.ts:370 and changed-files.ts:110 build `{ sessionId: 'code-review', ... }` deps for direct execution. [files: src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, src/analyze/context/driver.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts, src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts]","action":"Optional: when setting caller, note in the plan that deps pass through read-only-tool-loop.ts:80, which spreads args.deps, so the fields survive.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"approval.defaultAction and destructive.requireDoubleConfirm in tools/config.ts are read by nothing outside that file, so removing them is safe.","evidence":"A grep finds them only in config.ts (lines 30, 50, 74, 79, 109, 129 and 147; line 147 is a log field). The settings are reached outside the file only through updateToolSettings/getToolSettings at index.ts:1709-1716. The builtins read only notify, shell and web settings (notify/index.ts, shell/exec.ts:64, web/index.ts:66). [files: src/daemon/tools/config.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"tools.commonApproval becomes the only tool-approval setting: the design removes the old ones because 'a second common-class setting would conflict with this one'.","evidence":"The config catalog already has a tool permission setting that the LLD does not mention: config-catalog.ts:87 `{ path: 'permissions.mode', type: 'enum', default: 'validate', desc: \"tool permission mode: 'validate' | 'auto-accept'\", ... }`, typed at shared/types.ts:492 and surfaced in vscode-plugin/package.json:201 as insrc.permissions.mode. Nothing in src reads it at runtime. The design would leave two user-visible tool approval settings, which is the conflict it says it removes. [files: src/config/config-catalog.ts, src/shared/types.ts, vscode-plugin/package.json]","action":"Decide what happens to permissions.mode: retire it and migrate it into tools.commonApproval (for example auto-accept→auto, validate→manual), or state why it stays separate. Add it to the §3.5 call sites.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"IpcClient has no streaming method, so one is added as an optional member and the existing test doubles keep compiling.","evidence":"ipc-client.ts:121-138: the IpcClient interface has only rpc, status, reachability, update and updateOutcome. A new optional member would not break the doubles in per-role-engine.test.ts, registrar.test.ts, activation.test.ts or controller.test.ts. The design lists these and the files exist. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Outside the builtins, src/docgen/tool.ts is the only Tool that declares requiresApproval, and types.ts and executor.ts are the only other readers.","evidence":"A grep for `requiresApproval` outside builtins/** returns only docgen/tool.ts:56 (`requiresApproval: false`), executor.ts:12 (a comment) and :41-42, and types.ts:118. [files: src/docgen/tool.ts, src/daemon/tools/types.ts, src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The Tool type carries requiresApproval and destructive at types.ts:110-128, and ToolDeps at 50-81 has no caller or approval-mode field.","evidence":"types.ts:118 has `readonly requiresApproval?: boolean | ((input: ToolInput) => boolean);` and :128 has `readonly destructive?: boolean;`. The ToolDeps interface (50-81) has sessionId, repoPath, send, requestId, signal, todos, ollamaProvider and closureRepos, and no caller field. ToolApprovalGate (83-94) has title, content and actions, matching §2.4. [files: src/daemon/tools/types.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"tools.commonApproval can be an enum entry in the on-disk config catalog: stored in config.json, filled at boot, with a default.","evidence":"config-catalog.ts:32 allows `type: 'string' | 'number' | 'boolean' | 'enum'`, and :37-39 require enumValues on every enum row. Existing enum rows include logLevel (:79) and models.coreFloor (:113). config-boot-reconcile.test.ts:84 shows catalog defaults filled at boot (permissions.mode → 'validate'). [files: src/config/config-catalog.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/config-boot-reconcile.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The pending table is in memory only, so no stored records or migration are needed and nothing is persisted across a restart.","evidence":"§3.4 and §7 state 'Data rewrite: no', and the broker is a new in-memory map. No existing approval state is stored anywhere: the executor has no gate store (executor.ts:9-15 says the dispatcher was removed). The only removed persisted-adjacent fields are in the in-memory ToolSettings snapshot (config.ts:93 `let current = defaults()`). [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts, src/daemon/tools/config.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new denial reason 'cancelled' is raised as an amendment on s2's sc5 and not redesigned inside s3.","evidence":"AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-5.json: type sharedContract.fieldAdd, contractId sc5, \"type ToolDenialReason = 'declined' | 'timed-out' | 'no-client' | 'cancelled'\", proposedBy design.story s3, status draft. The LLD says it must be approved before the s3 build. The tool-call IPC method is left to s7, and only its request fields are defined here, in line with the round-3 finding 6 decision in tool-registry.md. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-5.json, docs/plans/tool-registry.md]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"'Every subscribed client disconnects' can be detected: the server aborts each subscribe handler's signal when its socket closes.","evidence":"server.ts:264-267: `const onClose = (): void => { abortController.abort(); }; socket.on('close', onClose); socket.on('error', onError);`. The signal is passed to the handler at :282, so the broker can drop the stream from its set and count it. A failed write also aborts (:275-277). [files: src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every acceptance criterion ac1–ac7 maps to at least one named test, and the plugin-side test path runs under the plugin's own node:test runner.","evidence":"Every row of the LLD acceptance mapping (ac1–ac7) names test files and titles. vscode-plugin/package.json:841 has `\"test\": \"tsx --test 'src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts'\"`, so vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/approval-subscribe.test.ts is picked up, and the root sweep glob covers the src/daemon/tools/__tests__ and src/cli/services/__tests__ files. The chat already has a similar test, vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/approval-queue.test.ts. [files: vscode-plugin/package.json]","action":"Optional: in the plan, say whether the chat approval UI reuses the existing approval queue (vscode-plugin/src/chat/approval-queue.ts) so the tests target it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T11:52:23.157Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
