11598	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s3","entry":{"id":"review-7ba90bbba5313f854ca1daacce9fa851","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T11:56:25.927Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"DEF s3 ac1–ac7 and FR001/FR002 are each designed: destructive always asks (ac1, ac2, ac5), no-client/timeout/decline deny (ac3, ac4), common class follows the effective mode (ac6), and the subscribe/answer exchange is built (ac7, FR002); the request names tool, repository and arguments (FR001).","evidence":"DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json:340-417 lists ac1–ac7 and FR001 'The approval request names the tool, the repository and the arguments'. LLD §2.1/§3.3 ApprovalRequest carries toolId, repoPath and arguments; §5 covers no-client, timed-out, declined and late answer; the acceptance mapping covers ac1–ac7.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac6 ('a tool that today declares it needs approval … asks for approval before it runs') is met by the common class asking only in manual/edit-auto, with the global default 'auto'.","evidence":"The literal DEF ac6 text is unamended. docs/plans/tool-registry.md:114-116 records the decision ('Default for the flag: `auto` (confirmed by the user)… a common call asks in `manual` and `edit-auto`, and does not ask in `auto`'), and the LLD follows it. Commit f24619f3 says the ac6 DEF amendment is to be raised at the start of s3. No such DEF amendment exists yet; the LLD records it only as an open question.","action":"Before the s3 build, file the agreed DEF s3 ac6 rewording ('asks when the effective mode says ask; destructive always asks') so the DEF matches the design.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.3","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"No non-goal is built: there is no allow-all for destructive calls and no approval when nobody answers.","evidence":"DEF non-goal at :136-137 'A blanket allow-all for destructive operations, or approving them when no client answers'. LLD §2.1 resolves 'no-client' at once and 'timed-out' at expiry. §5 edge cases say destructive asks whatever the approvalMode or caller.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"executeTool (executor.ts:41-48) treats requiresApproval (true or a predicate) as approved, logs 'auto-approving' and runs the tool.","evidence":"executor.ts:41-45: `const needsGate = tool.requiresApproval === true || (typeof … === 'function' && tool.requiresApproval(input)); if (needsGate) log.warn(…'auto-approving')`, then at :48 `return await tool.execute(input, deps)`. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The IPC server pushes only over a client-opened stream, aborts the stream handler's signal when the socket closes, and IpcStreamKind already has 'gate'. gate.request-permission is an offline stub.","evidence":"server.ts:261-267: an AbortController is aborted on socket 'close'/'error' and passed to handler(params, sendStream, signal). types.ts:905 IpcStreamKind includes 'gate'. index.ts:1931 `'gate.request-permission': offlineStream('gate.request-permission')`. [files: src/daemon/server.ts, src/shared/types.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"approval.defaultAction and destructive.requireDoubleConfirm in src/daemon/tools/config.ts are read by nothing outside that file, and permissions.mode is read by nothing at runtime.","evidence":"A grep for defaultAction/requireDoubleConfirm finds only config.ts:30,50,74,79,109,129,147 (147 is a log field inside the same file). A grep for permissions.mode/.permissions in src and vscode-plugin/src finds only the catalog entry (config-catalog.ts:87), the type (shared/types.ts:491) and tests. [files: src/daemon/tools/config.ts, src/config/config-catalog.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Exactly eight builtins set destructive: true today, and they are mapped to the destructive class.","evidence":"A grep for 'destructive:\\s*true' finds 8: az/vm.ts:238, aws/s3.ts:210, aws/cloudformation.ts:235, aws/ec2.ts:255, gcp/storage.ts:189, gcp/compute.ts:247, gcp/run.ts:212, k8s/index.ts:340. [files: src/daemon/tools/builtins]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"IpcClient in src/shared/ipc-client.ts has no streaming member today, the vscode-plugin reaches the daemon through it, and the listed test doubles implement it structurally (so a new member must be optional).","evidence":"ipc-client.ts:121-138 has rpc/status/reachability/update/updateOutcome and no stream method. `const fakeClient: IpcClient = {` at per-role-engine.test.ts:145 and registrar.test.ts:16, plus doubles in controller.test.ts:30 and activation.test.ts:29,138. extension.ts, activation.ts, controller.ts and docs-review-client.ts consume IpcClient. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts, vscode-plugin/src/config/__tests__/per-role-engine.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/workspace/__tests__/registrar.test.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Of the ToolDeps builders, only driver.ts and ollama.ts reach executeTool, and grounding.ts and changed-files.ts call execute directly.","evidence":"executeTool's only production caller is read-only-tool-loop.ts:78. runReadOnlyToolLoop is called from driver.ts:875 (deps from buildToolDeps :1114) and ollama.ts:681 (inline deps at :686). grounding.ts:370 and changed-files.ts:110 build ToolDeps literals for a direct execute. [files: src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts, src/analyze/context/driver.ts, src/agent/providers/ollama.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The change-site inventory for retiring permissions.mode (§3.5, migration step 2) is complete: config-catalog.ts, config.ts, shared/types.ts and vscode-plugin/package.json.","evidence":"Existing tests assert the current state and will fail once permissions.mode joins RETIRED_PATHS. src/config/__tests__/config-catalog-contract.test.ts:106 has `test('RETIRED_PATHS covers exactly the 6 declared legacy entries…')`, and src/daemon/__tests__/config-boot-reconcile.test.ts:84 has `assert.equal(getPath(firstBoot, 'permissions.mode'), 'validate')`. site/settings.html:58 also documents `permissions.mode`. None of these is named in the LLD's call sites or migration steps. [files: src/config/__tests__/config-catalog-contract.test.ts, src/daemon/__tests__/config-boot-reconcile.test.ts, site/settings.html]","action":"Add these to step 2's change sites: update the RETIRED_PATHS count test to 7, change the boot-reconcile assertion to tools.commonApproval === 'auto' (and permissions.mode pruned), and drop permissions.mode from site/settings.html.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Stored config is handled: tools.commonApproval is a catalog enum filled by the boot reconcile, and a stored permissions.mode is stripped through RETIRED_PATHS with no migration.","evidence":"config-catalog.ts:148 exports RETIRED_PATHS, which reconcile.ts:331 applies. Catalog entries support `type: 'enum'` with enumValues (config-catalog.ts:87). The approval pending table is in-memory only, and §3.4 states it is lost on restart. [files: src/config/config-catalog.ts, src/config/reconcile.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"s3 does not classify git/gh/Jira operations as destructive (owned by s4/s5/s6), does not build the tool-call IPC (owned by s7), and uses s2's ToolFailure 'denied' with the 'cancelled' reason raised as amendment AMD-5 rather than redesigning sc5.","evidence":"The LLD maps only the existing 8 destructive:true builtins. git push/reset keep requiresApproval→common. AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-5.json:41-42 proposes `ToolDenialReason = 'declined' | 'timed-out' | 'no-client' | 'cancelled'` (status draft). §4 states that s7 builds the tool-call IPC method against s3's caller/approvalMode fields. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-5.json]","action":"Approve AMD-5 (and the sc4 refinement AMD-4) before the s3 build, as the LLD states.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An abort of every subscriber can be detected because each subscribe handler's signal fires on socket close, so the broker can resolve pending requests to 'no-client'.","evidence":"server.ts:264-267 `const onClose = (): void => { abortController.abort(); }; socket.on('close', onClose);` and the signal is passed to the stream handler at :282. [files: src/daemon/server.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"executeTool never throws, and approval failures return a failed ToolResult.","evidence":"executor.ts:28-58 returns success:false for an unknown tool and for a thrown execute. The LLD keeps this invariant and adds denial as a failed result, a throwing class function as destructive, and a throwing buildApprovalGate as a generic preview. [files: src/daemon/tools/executor.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each of ac1–ac7 maps to at least one named test, including the terminal-client and editor/chat client sides for ac6/ac7.","evidence":"LLD §6 acceptance mapping lists approval-broker, approval-ipc, executor-approval and approval-class-mapping tests under src/daemon/tools/__tests__, plus src/cli/services/__tests__/approval-subscribe.test.ts and vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/approval-subscribe.test.ts. Each criterion has at least one test.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T11:56:25.927Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
