11592	{"artifactId":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s3","entry":{"id":"review-a982ec6bb275bdf1397901f08c48c3f3","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-23T11:58:28.997Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"DEF s3 ac6 (a tool that today declares it needs approval asks before it runs, in the terminal client, the editor and a chat) is designed.","evidence":"DEF line 391-397 ac6: given 'a tool that today declares it needs approval and is run as if approved', then 'it asks for approval before it runs'. The LLD maps requiresApproval:true to 'common', and the common class follows tools.commonApproval with default 'auto', so under the default these tools still run without asking (§7 Backward compat: 'Under the default auto mode common calls still run without asking'). The LLD says this reading is 'recorded here only' (§10). Of the amendments AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-4..7, none mentions ac6; all are drafts. The latest commit message (f24619f3) says the ac6 DEF amendment is to be raised at the start of s3. [files: .insrc/artifacts/DEF-b7a68147dcf72034.json, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s3.json]","action":"Raise the DEF amendment that rewrites s3 ac6 to the effective-mode reading (manual/edit-auto ask; destructive always asks), or make the default ask. Do this before the LLD is approved, so ac6 and the design agree.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Non-goal 'approving destructive operations when no client answers' and k5 'no global opt-in' are respected: the destructive class reads neither the setting nor the caller fields.","evidence":"DEF lines 136 and 197. The LLD resolves 'no-client' and 'timed-out' to a denial (§2.1, §5). tools.commonApproval and deps.approvalMode apply to the common class only ('never read for the destructive class'). requireDoubleConfirm, the only existing destructive setting (src/daemon/tools/config.ts:50), is removed.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"executeTool at executor.ts:41-48 treats requiresApproval (true or a predicate) as approved, logs 'auto-approving' and runs the tool.","evidence":"src/daemon/tools/executor.ts:41-48: needsGate = requiresApproval === true || predicate(input); if needsGate, log.warn('...gate dispatcher is gone; auto-approving'), then 'return await tool.execute(input, deps)'.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The IPC server can push only over a stream the client opened, and it aborts a stream handler's signal when the socket closes (relied on by the 'every subscriber disconnects' error path). IpcStreamKind already has 'gate', and gate.request-permission is an offline stub.","evidence":"src/daemon/server.ts:260-267: an AbortController per stream request, with socket.on('close'/'error') → abortController.abort(), and the signal passed to the handler at :282. src/shared/types.ts:905 IpcStreamKind includes 'gate'. src/daemon/index.ts:1931: 'gate.request-permission': offlineStream(...).","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"approval.defaultAction and destructive.requireDoubleConfirm in src/daemon/tools/config.ts are read by nothing outside that file, and permissions.mode is read by nothing at runtime.","evidence":"A grep for defaultAction/requireDoubleConfirm finds them only in src/daemon/tools/config.ts. getToolSettings() callers read only .web, .shell and .notify (web/index.ts:66, shell/exec.ts:64,109, notify/index.ts). index.ts:1716 returns the whole snapshot over tools.config.get, but no consumer reads the approval fields. permissions.mode appears only in config-catalog.ts:87, shared/types.ts:491, tests and fixtures, site/settings.html and vscode-plugin/package.json:201. No runtime reader was found.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The broker, approval.subscribe, approval.answer and ApprovalClass are new; Tool.buildApprovalGate exists with a title/content/actions shape and is reused as the preview source.","evidence":"There are no approval.subscribe or approval.answer handlers in index.ts; the stream handler map at :1924-1937 has only offline stubs and todos.subscribe. src/daemon/tools/types.ts:83-94 ToolApprovalGate { title; content; actions }, and :145 buildApprovalGate?(input): ToolApprovalGate | Promise<ToolApprovalGate>.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"IpcClient in src/shared/ipc-client.ts has no streaming method today, so adding an optional one is new.","evidence":"src/shared/ipc-client.ts:121-138: IpcClient has rpc, status, reachability, update and updateOutcome, and no stream member.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Eight builtins declare destructive: true.","evidence":"A grep for 'destructive:\\s*true' under src finds exactly 8: az/vm.ts:238, gcp/storage.ts:189, gcp/compute.ts:247, gcp/run.ts:212, k8s/index.ts:340, aws/cloudformation.ts:235, aws/ec2.ts:255, aws/s3.ts:210.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"There are 77 'requiresApproval: false' declarations across 55 files (including src/docgen/tool.ts, the one non-builtin Tool).","evidence":"The count grep for 'requiresApproval:\\s*false' reports 'Found 77 total occurrences across 55 files', and src/docgen/tool.ts:1 is among them. That is 55 files, not 55 tools: it includes docgen/tool.ts.","action":"None. Optionally reword it as '55 files'.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Of the four ToolDeps builders, only driver.ts and ollama.ts reach executeTool; grounding.ts and changed-files.ts call git_diff's execute directly.","evidence":"executeTool is called only from src/agent/read-only-tool-loop.ts:78, which is used by src/analyze/context/driver.ts:875 (buildToolDeps at :1114) and src/agent/providers/ollama.ts:681. src/workflow/code-review/grounding.ts:370-371 and src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts:110-111 build ToolDeps literals and call gitDiffTool.execute directly. The LLD's driver.ts:1132 is approximate; buildToolDeps is at :1114.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.4","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Retiring permissions.mode needs only the listed test updates: the RETIRED_PATHS count in config-catalog-contract.test.ts (6→7) and the permissions.mode assertion in config-boot-reconcile.test.ts.","evidence":"src/config/__tests__/config-reconcile-smoke.test.ts:89: assert.deepEqual(written['permissions'], literal['permissions']), where the fixture daemon-defaults-literal.json:6-8 holds { \"permissions\": { \"mode\": \"validate\" } }. Once permissions.mode is retired, first boot no longer writes it, so this assertion fails. Neither the test nor the fixture is in §3.5's call sites or migration step 2. fixtures/PROVENANCE.md:16 also names permissions.mode as surviving. [files: src/config/__tests__/config-reconcile-smoke.test.ts, src/config/__tests__/fixtures/daemon-defaults-literal.json, src/config/__tests__/fixtures/PROVENANCE.md]","action":"Add config-reconcile-smoke.test.ts (assert that permissions is absent, or drop the line), the daemon-defaults-literal fixture handling, and the PROVENANCE note to §3.5 and migration step 2.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Stored configs carrying permissions.mode are pruned through RETIRED_PATHS by the boot reconcile, the new key is filled with its default, and pending approvals are in memory only, so nothing persisted needs migrating.","evidence":"src/config/reconcile.ts:331 reconcile takes retired = RETIRED_PATHS and prunes them. config-catalog.ts:148 defines RETIRED_PATHS. Catalog entries are filled with their defaults at boot (config-boot-reconcile.test.ts:84 shows permissions.mode being filled the same way). §3.4 has the broker in memory, with restart treated as a denial.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"s3 consumes s2's ToolFailure/ToolDenialReason rather than redefining them, and routes the extra 'cancelled' value through an sc5 amendment.","evidence":"LLD-b7a68147dcf72034-s2.json:449 adds ToolDenialReason ('declined' | 'timed-out' | 'no-client') per AMD-…-3. AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-5.json:41-42 proposes ToolDenialReason with 'cancelled' added and is in draft. s3 §4 says it must be approved before the build. The tool-call IPC is left to s7, with only its sc4-owned request fields defined here.","action":"Make sure AMD-b7a68147dcf72034-5 is approved before the s3 build, as the LLD states.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Disconnect of all subscribers is detectable: the server aborts each subscribe handler's signal when its socket closes, so the broker can track the open-stream count.","evidence":"src/daemon/server.ts:264-267 abort on 'close' and 'error', and :277 aborts on a write failure. The signal is passed to the handler at :282. A long-lived subscribe handler can await the abort and decrement the count.","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion ac1-ac7 maps to at least one named test case.","evidence":"The §6 acceptance mapping lists proving tests for ac1, ac2, ac3, ac4, ac5, ac6 and ac7, which matches DEF s3 ac1-ac7 (DEF lines 345-407). ac6 and ac7 include the terminal-client (src/cli/services/__tests__) and editor/chat (vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__) tests. The tests prove the design's effective-mode reading of ac6, not the DEF's literal text (see coverage-of-intent).","action":"None beyond the ac6 amendment.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":13,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-23T11:58:28.997Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
